.TH PRESET 1.SH NAMEpreset \- load a terminal's function keys.SH SYNOPSIS\fBpreset\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBpreset\fRwrites the control string that programs a terminal's function keys witha fixed set of commands -- among them\fBdir\fR,\fR\fBumacs\fR,\fR\fBr68\fR,\fR\fBl68\fRand\fBdsave \-ieb128k\fR-- and answers, in German,\fBFunktionstasten belegt!\fR:\fRthe keys are set.  The definitions are built into it; it takes noarguments and ignores any given.  To choose your own, use\fBfkeys\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOfkeys, chardef